      "writtenOn": "2021-09-01T10:30:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think this answers Lorenzo\u0027s question ; given that disconnectAndDestroyNetwork is always called on the handler thread but removes the NAI from the map, how can this code be called at all with an already-destroyed network ?\n\nI think the answer to this is in updateNetworkInfo ; updateNetworkInfo is called with the argument in a message, which is initialized with `this` in NetworkAgentRegistry. That means I think it\u0027s technically possible that CS calls tearDownUnneededNetwork, calling nai.disconnect() and queuing up a message to call this, but before it\u0027s done the NA calls sendNetworkInfo with DISCONNECTED, which never looks up the agent from the map.\n\nIf that\u0027s true, then it\u0027s indeed a bug in ConnectivityService, and the simplest fix is to change\n\n  if (mNetworkAgentInfos.contains(nai)) {\n    disconnectAndDestroyNetwork(nai);\n  }\n\n...in handleNetworkAgentDisconnected to\n\n  if (!mNetworkAgentInfo.contains(nai)) return;\n\n...to the top of this method. It\u0027s simpler because otherwise we\u0027d have to protect both calls in the same way.",
      "parentUuid": "8f091df3_1f12dbee",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 3942,
        "startChar": 86,
        "endLine": 3943,
        "endChar": 42
      },
